{
  "subevents": [
    {
      "id": "0",
      "subevent": "A mortar attack occurred in northern Faryab province on Thursday morning."
    },
    {
      "id": "1",
      "subevent": "At least four civilians were killed and 10 others were wounded in the attack."
    },
    {
      "id": "2",
      "subevent": "The incident happened around 11:00am local time after a mortar round landed in a market in Shareen Tagab district."
    },
    {
      "id": "3",
      "subevent": "Abdul Karim Yourish, a spokesman for the provincial police chief, said the mortar was fired 'by the Taliban' to target security forces."
    },
    {
      "id": "4",
      "subevent": "Yourish added that all the victims were civilians who were at the market to shop."
    },
    {
      "id": "5",
      "subevent": "The Taliban has not commented on the attack."
    }
  ]
}

{
  "subevents": [
    {
      "id": "0",
      "subevent": "Economy Minister Roberto Gualtieri said that Confindustria's forecast of a 6% fall in gross domestic product this year due to the coronavirus crisis is realistic."
    },
    {
      "id": "1",
      "subevent": "On Tuesday, national business association Confindustria said the outbreak would cause a serious recession in 2020."
    },
    {
      "id": "2",
      "subevent": "Gualtieri told Il Fatto Quotidiano that the estimates are realistic and the Italian economy can aim for a vigorous rebound."
    },
    {
      "id": "3",
      "subevent": "The government is not due to give its own estimates of the impact until the end of April when it publishes the Document of Economy and Finance."
    },
    {
      "id": "4",
      "subevent": "Italy's output rose 0.3% last year, and the government expected it to grow 0.6% this year before the coronavirus emerged at the end of February."
    },
    {
      "id": "5",
      "subevent": "At the end of March, two sources told Reuters that the Treasury expected the economy to contract around 3% this year."
    },
    {
      "id": "6",
      "subevent": "Gualtieri said a new stimulus package, set to be approved this month, will be significantly larger than the 25 billion euros passed in March and sufficient for the entire epidemic."
    },
    {
      "id": "7",
      "subevent": "He said it will include an extension of state-backed guarantees for companies seeking liquidity, unemployment benefits, and support for people on low incomes."
    },
    {
      "id": "8",
      "subevent": "Gualtieri said using the European Stability Mechanism under current conditions is not an option and that Europe needs a coordinated shared fiscal policy."
    },
    {
      "id": "9",
      "subevent": "He said new solutions are needed to grant parity of conditions and define an adequate shared and responsible response."
    }
  ]
}

{
  "subevents": [
    {
      "id": "0",
      "subevent": "Yoshiro Mori resigned as president of the Tokyo Olympic Committee after making sexist remarks about women."
    },
    {
      "id": "1",
      "subevent": "Mori announced his resignation at a meeting of the Olympic Committee's executive board and council."
    },
    {
      "id": "2",
      "subevent": "Mori had reportedly said women talk too much and have a strong sense of rivalry during a board meeting."
    },
    {
      "id": "3",
      "subevent": "After criticism, Mori apologized and retracted his remarks, acknowledging they were inappropriate."
    },
    {
      "id": "4",
      "subevent": "Mori apologized again while announcing his resignation, saying his comments caused big trouble."
    },
    {
      "id": "5",
      "subevent": "Mori stated that his comments were misinterpreted and that he was not prejudiced against women."
    },
    {
      "id": "6",
      "subevent": "IOC President Thomas Bach said the IOC respects Mori's decision and will work with his successor."
    },
    {
      "id": "7",
      "subevent": "Japan extended its state of emergency in Tokyo and other regions by another month due to COVID-19."
    },
    {
      "id": "8",
      "subevent": "Japan reported its worst one-day death toll for COVID-19 with 121 new deaths and has not started mass vaccinations."
    },
    {
      "id": "9",
      "subevent": "Nearly 80% of the Japanese public said the Olympics should be canceled or further delayed."
    },
    {
      "id": "10",
      "subevent": "Hundreds of Olympic volunteers quit and local organizers received thousands of complaints after Mori's remarks."
    },
    {
      "id": "11",
      "subevent": "Tennis player Naomi Osaka called Mori's comments 'really ignorant' and swimmer Kosuke Hagino called them 'very unfortunate.'"
    },
    {
      "id": "12",
      "subevent": "Several sponsors voiced concerns over Mori's remarks."
    },
    {
      "id": "13",
      "subevent": "Female opposition lawmakers wore white with roses in protest of Mori's remarks."
    },
    {
      "id": "14",
      "subevent": "Japan ranked 121st out of 153 countries in the World Economic Forum's 2020 gender gap index."
    }
  ]
}

{
  "subevents": [
    {
      "id": "0",
      "subevent": "Biomerieux gave its proprietary formula to the Canadian government for free."
    },
    {
      "id": "1",
      "subevent": "In March, Canada passed emergency legislation giving the government and third parties the right to produce patented goods without consent."
    },
    {
      "id": "2",
      "subevent": "Canada did not force Biomerieux to agree, but the option was available."
    },
    {
      "id": "3",
      "subevent": "Biomerieux did not respond to questions about similar arrangements with other governments or the revenue impact."
    },
    {
      "id": "4",
      "subevent": "Biomerieux reported a 21.5% increase in first-quarter sales due in part to demand for reagent."
    },
    {
      "id": "5",
      "subevent": "The Public Health Agency of Canada described the arrangement as a temporary license at no cost."
    },
    {
      "id": "6",
      "subevent": "PHAC said its manufacturing was in development and testing, aiming to alleviate shortages soon."
    },
    {
      "id": "7",
      "subevent": "Biomerieux's Canadian unit emailed customers in early April saying the move clears testing backlogs and it is boosting own production."
    },
    {
      "id": "8",
      "subevent": "The chemicals in short supply are reagents used to extract RNA from patient samples."
    },
    {
      "id": "9",
      "subevent": "Biomerieux extraction equipment is widely used in Canada, primarily in Ontario, contributing to a testing slowdown in late March."
    },
    {
      "id": "10",
      "subevent": "PHAC said the deal is an interim solution because its facilities are not for long-term manufacturing."
    },
    {
      "id": "11",
      "subevent": "On Thursday, Canada pledged C$1.1 billion for research and drug or vaccine manufacturing."
    }
  ]
}

